# LF everywhere, even where Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true would
# check files out as CRLF. Git Bash shrugs off a CR, but a WSL shell running a
# clone that Windows' git made -- on /mnt/c, say -- dies on the shebang
# ("bash\r: No such file or directory"), and the policy text the installer
# splices into CLAUDE.md would carry the CRs along.
* text=auto eol=lf
